# Optional: point the front-end at the Node backend instead of localStorage.
# Leave unset for the zero-config demo (data persists in the browser).
# VITE_API_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assistant (the /dashboard/assistant page)
#
# NOTE THE MISSING "VITE_" PREFIX — that is deliberate and important.
# Anything named VITE_* is compiled into the browser bundle and is readable by
# every visitor to the site. These are read only by the serverless function at
# api/chat.js, so the key never leaves the server.
#
# Set these in the Vercel dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables)
# for production, or here in .env.local for local development.
#
# Without a key the assistant still runs: it falls back to a built-in scripted
# flow that asks the same questions and produces the same priced draft, just
# with plainer wording. Nothing breaks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# MT Asphalt's own DeepSeek key — recommended for production.
# Get one at https://platform.deepseek.com
# AI_API_KEY=sk-...
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# AI_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash

# Alternative: an OpenCode Go key (any OpenAI-compatible provider works).
# Fine for development. Not recommended for Michael's production use — the
# usage caps are shared across your whole account, so heavy coding on your side
# takes his contracts offline mid-job.
# AI_API_KEY=...
# AI_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1
# AI_MODEL=deepseek-v4-prohttp://localhost:8787

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard sign-in (Google OAuth, server-only)
#
# The dashboard no longer uses a shared password — signing in requires a
# Google account, and only emails on the admin allowlist get past
# api/auth/google-callback.js. Michael's own address is always allowed (see
# BASE_ADMIN_EMAILS in api/_auth-helpers.js); ADMIN_EMAILS adds more.
#
# Step-by-step Google Cloud Console setup: see MICHAEL_GUIDE.md.
#
# NOTE: no "VITE_" prefix on any of these — they're read only by the
# serverless functions under api/auth/ and must never reach the browser
# bundle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# From Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID
# (type: Web application). Authorized redirect URI must be exactly
# <your-domain>/api/auth/google-callback (and http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google-callback
# for local `vercel dev` testing).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Extra approved admin emails beyond the built-in owner address, comma-
# separated. Example: ADMIN_EMAILS=someone@gmail.com,another@gmail.com
# ADMIN_EMAILS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret (server-only, required in production)
#
# Signs the dashboard's login session tokens (HMAC + expiry) so /api/data can
# verify a token without a storage round-trip. Any long random string works —
# generate one with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Without it, tokens fall back to a fixed non-secret local-dev key — fine for
# local dev, not for production (set it in Vercel → Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SESSION_SECRET=
